course: dictionary
lesson: 5127
title: Inventor
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An inventor is a person who thinks of and makes something new that did not exist before. Look at the words around the word for clues. «Inventors build on earlier ideas: the bicycle needed the wheel, and the car needed both the wheel and the engine.» Old ideas help inventors make new things.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «Many inventors made electric light bulbs before Edison, including Joseph Swan in England» still makes sense if inventors means people who thought of and made bulbs. Clue words like made, thought of and before tell you that inventors create and try things.
explain: An invention can be improved by a team. «Edison's team at Menlo Park made a long-lasting, practical bulb and a whole system to power it.» The word team shows that inventing is not always the work of one person.
fact: An inventor is a person who thinks of and makes something new.
fact: Inventions often build on earlier ideas: the wheel helped make both the bicycle and the car.
fact: Alexander Graham Bell was an inventor who is known for the telephone.
fact: The Wright brothers were inventors who made the aeroplane.
fact: Inventors often try many times before an idea works well.
exercise: What is an inventor? | Someone who sells old things in a shop | *Someone who thinks of and makes something new | Someone who paints pictures of animals | Someone who only fixes broken machines
exercise: «Many inventors made electric light bulbs before Edison, including Joseph Swan in England.» Find and copy one word that means a person who invents. | bulbs | England | Edison | *inventors
exercise: «Inventors build on earlier ideas: the car needed both the wheel and the engine.» What does this tell you about inventions? | They are always finished in one day | *They often build on ideas that already existed | Cars were invented before wheels | Inventors never use old ideas
test: According to the example, which two things did the car need? | A bicycle and a bulb | *The wheel and the engine | A road and a bridge | The telephone and the aeroplane
test: Who is known for inventing the telephone? | Isaac Newton | Queen Victoria | *Alexander Graham Bell | The Wright brothers
exam: «Edison's team at Menlo Park made a long-lasting, practical bulb.» Which word tells you that Edison did not work alone? | *team | long-lasting | practical | bulb
